From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 06 Sep 2026 23:16:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-input-hid: send BTN_TOUCH for the tablet, so Android
 sees a touchscreen

DomA (AAOS) gets no touch input from virtio-tablet-pci. Android classifies an
ABS_X/ABS_Y device as a touchscreen only when it also reports BTN_TOUCH; a
device that reports BTN_LEFT instead is an absolute pointer, and the guest's
input stack then routes nothing to the UI -- no clicks from a mouse, nothing
from a real touch panel.

This is the qemu 10.0.2 form of the fix meta-xt-driver-domain carries for the
7.0.0-xt device model as 0111 (Leonid Komarianskyi). That patch needed three
pieces; on 10.0.2 upstream already has two of them:

  * qapi/ui.json's InputButton enum already includes 'touch';
  * keymap_button already has [INPUT_BUTTON_TOUCH] = BTN_TOUCH.

and the second of those is what makes the tablet ADVERTISE BTN_TOUCH already:
its EV_KEY bitmap is not a literal in virtio_tablet_config_v1/v2 -- neither
declares EV_KEY at all -- it is synthesised from the whole keymap_button array by
virtio_input_extend_config(vinput, keymap_button, ..., EV_BITS, EV_KEY) in
virtio_tablet_init(). So the guest's evdev device already has BTN_TOUCH in its
key bitmap and would not filter the event out.

What is missing on 10.0.2 is only the send side: a left press arrives as
INPUT_BUTTON_LEFT and goes out as BTN_LEFT. Hence this patch is the remap alone,
with no capability or config-space change -- three lines of logic where 0111
needed a QAPI enum extension and a keymap entry as well.

Two notes on the shape:

  * `vhid->handler` is `const QemuInputHandler *` in 10.0.2, so the cast 0111
    used is gone rather than casting const away. The handler is matched by name
    because virtio_tablet_handler is defined below this function; comparing the
    pointer would need a forward declaration for no gain.

  * The remap is unconditional for the tablet, not behind a property. That is
    what the device is for on this platform, and the same unconditional remap
    has shipped in the 7.0.0 lane with BOTH guests on virtio-tablet-pci --
    including the AGL DomU, whose compositor keeps working: libinput then treats
    the device as a touchscreen rather than an absolute pointer, which is what a
    kiosk UI wants. Making it conditional would add a knob whose only correct
    setting is "on".

Why it is needed here at all: the Venus lane moves the device model from
7.0.0-xt to 10.0.2, which version-gates the six 7.0.0-only patches off, 0111
among them -- so without this patch a Venus DomA gets no touch input.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [same downstream policy as the 7.0.0 original;
 upstream's answer is for the front end to emit INPUT_BUTTON_TOUCH, which SDL's
 mouse path does not]
---
 hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c b/hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c
index 812faae..c5f35e1 100644
--- a/hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c
+++ b/hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c
@@ -89,6 +89,30 @@ static void virtio_input_handle_event(DeviceState *dev, QemuConsole *src,
     InputMoveEvent *move;
     InputBtnEvent *btn;
     InputMultiTouchEvent *mtt;
+    /*
+     * Android classifies an ABS_X/ABS_Y device as a touchscreen only when it
+     * also reports BTN_TOUCH; with BTN_LEFT it is an absolute pointer and the
+     * guest's input stack routes nothing to the UI. See
+     * source.android.com/docs/core/interaction/input/touch-devices
+     * (section "Touch device classification").
+     *
+     * The tablet already ADVERTISES BTN_TOUCH: its EV_KEY bitmap is synthesised
+     * from keymap_button by virtio_input_extend_config() below, and that map
+     * has carried [INPUT_BUTTON_TOUCH] = BTN_TOUCH since the enum gained
+     * 'touch'. What it does not do is send it -- a left press arrives as
+     * INPUT_BUTTON_LEFT and goes out as BTN_LEFT. So this is a send-side remap
+     * only; no capability changes and no config-space change, which is why it
+     * is three lines here.
+     *
+     * Deliberately not conditional on a device property: it is what the tablet
+     * is for on this platform, and the same remap has shipped in the 7.0.0 fork
+     * with both guests using virtio-tablet-pci, including the AGL DomU whose
+     * compositor keeps working (libinput then treats the device as a
+     * touchscreen rather than an absolute pointer, which is what a kiosk UI
+     * wants anyway).
+     */
+    bool is_tablet = vhid->handler && vhid->handler->name &&
+                     !strcmp(vhid->handler->name, VIRTIO_ID_NAME_TABLET);
 
     switch (evt->type) {
     case INPUT_EVENT_KIND_KEY:
@@ -120,7 +144,11 @@ static void virtio_input_handle_event(DeviceState *dev, QemuConsole *src,
             virtio_input_send(vinput, &event);
         } else if (keymap_button[btn->button]) {
             event.type  = cpu_to_le16(EV_KEY);
-            event.code  = cpu_to_le16(keymap_button[btn->button]);
+            if (btn->button == INPUT_BUTTON_LEFT && is_tablet) {
+                event.code = cpu_to_le16(BTN_TOUCH);
+            } else {
+                event.code = cpu_to_le16(keymap_button[btn->button]);
+            }
             event.value = cpu_to_le32(btn->down ? 1 : 0);
             virtio_input_send(vinput, &event);
         } else {
